This product produces HF radio propagation forecasts from VOACAP, the
Voice of America Coverage Analysis Program.

VOACAP was developed by the Institute for Telecommunication Sciences
(ITS), National Telecommunications and Information Administration
(NTIA), United States Department of Commerce, and is maintained by
Greg Hand. As a work of the United States Government it is stated to
be not subject to copyright protection in the United States.

The Unix build of VOACAP, `voacapl`, and the changes it carries, are
by J.A. Watson, released under CC0 1.0 Universal.

The server drives one of two engines: `voacapl` itself, or the Rust
port of it in the hfcast-engine repository. Neither is included here.
The deck builder and listing parser in server/src/voacap/ were written
against VOACAP's documented input and output formats.

